diff --git a/utils/meta-intel-sdo/README.md b/utils/meta-intel-sdo/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cc7a7b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/utils/meta-intel-sdo/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# meta-intel-sdo
+
+This layer provides Yocto recipes for building the FIDO Device Onboard (FDO) Client SDK.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+This layer depends on:
+* `core` (meta-openembedded / OE-Core)
+
+The wolfSSL recipe (`clientsdk-wolfssl`) and the wolfSSL configure flags it needs live
+under `dynamic-layers/wolfssl/` and are only used when `meta-wolfssl` (the official wolfSSL
+Yocto layer) is also in `BBLAYERS`. The OpenSSL and mbedTLS recipes don't need it.
+
+Supported release series: dunfell (3.1.11 or later), kirkstone and scarthgap.
+
+## Automated Setup
+
+To make setup easier, a script is provided in the `utils` directory of the FDO Client SDK repository that will automatically clone the required `meta-wolfssl` layer into your Yocto environment.
+
+From the root of the FDO Client SDK repository, run:
+```bash
+./utils/setup_yocto_wolfssl.sh /path/to/your/yocto/dir
+```
+*(If no path is provided, it defaults to `~/yocto`)*
+
+## Manual Setup
+
+If you prefer to set up the dependencies manually:
+
+1. **Clone the official meta-wolfssl layer** alongside your other Yocto layers (like `poky`):
+   ```bash
+   git clone https://github.com/wolfSSL/meta-wolfssl.git
+   ```
+
+2. **Source your build environment:**
+   ```bash
+   source poky/oe-init-build-env build
+   ```
+
+3. **Add the layers to your `bblayers.conf`:**
+   ```bash
+   bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-wolfssl
+   bitbake-layers add-layer /path/to/client-sdk-fidoiot/utils/meta-intel-sdo
+   ```
+
+## Building
+
+Once your layers are configured, you can build the wolfSSL-backed FDO client:
+```bash
+bitbake clientsdk-wolfssl
+```
+
+`clientsdk-wolfssl` fetches upstream client-sdk-fidoiot at commit `40e5024` and applies
+the wolfSSL OSP patch. Before building, copy this file from
+[wolfSSL/osp](https://github.com/wolfSSL/osp):
+`client-sdk-fidoiot/2025-08-06-40e5024d46472020f3e7811dae9f40b0644c17f4.patch`
+into `dynamic-layers/wolfssl/recipes-connectivity/clientsdk-wolfssl/files/`.
+
+By default the image's curl still uses OpenSSL, so `linux-client` ends up linking both
+libraries. To build curl against wolfSSL too, so the client has no OpenSSL dependency,
+add to `local.conf`:
+```bash
+CLIENTSDK_WOLFSSL_CURL = "1"
+```
+This switches curl for every package in the image, which is why it is opt-in. Build-host
+(`-native`) curl is left on OpenSSL. Use this instead of meta-wolfssl's own
+`curl_%.bbappend`, which fails `do_configure` QA on scarthgap.
